From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 15:48:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] winex11: an expose does not say what is on top under a
 compositing manager.

When part of a window is exposed, the window was put above whatever the
Win32 side had over that part: on an X server that draws the screen itself,
that part has just come out from under another window.  With a compositing
manager every window has a pixmap of its own, exposed when the window is
mapped or grows and never because a window over it went away.

After a display change, every window resized at once and each one was put
above the others in turn, which turned the Z order over: the window with
the focus, on top on the screen, ended up at the bottom of the Win32 Z
order.  Under a compositing manager -- as always under Xwayland -- an expose
now only repaints.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 4be87be7934d0c6c4db527b80453401f1cfae26c)

diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
index 884814b3557..3443459f2f6 100644
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/event.c
@@ -829,6 +829,35 @@ static BOOL X11DRV_FocusOut( HWND hwnd, XEvent *xev )
 }
 
 
+/***********************************************************************
+ *           is_screen_composited
+ *
+ * Whether a compositing manager draws the screen, as it always does under
+ * Xwayland.  Every window then has a pixmap of its own: it is exposed when it
+ * is mapped or grows, and not when a window that covered it moves away, so an
+ * expose says nothing about what is on top.  Checked again at most once a
+ * second, as a compositing manager can come and go.
+ */
+static BOOL is_screen_composited( Display *display )
+{
+    static Atom selection;
+    static UINT checked;
+    static BOOL composited;
+    UINT now = NtGetTickCount();
+
+    if (checked && now - checked < 1000) return composited;
+    if (!selection)
+    {
+        char name[32];
+        snprintf( name, sizeof(name), "_NET_WM_CM_S%d", DefaultScreen( display ) );
+        selection = XInternAtom( display, name, False );
+    }
+    composited = XGetSelectionOwner( display, selection ) != None;
+    checked = now ? now : 1;
+    return composited;
+}
+
+
 /***********************************************************************
  *           X11DRV_Expose
  */
@@ -866,13 +895,20 @@ static BOOL X11DRV_Expose( HWND hwnd, XEvent *xev )
         abs_rect = rect;
         OffsetRect( &abs_rect, data->rects.client.left, data->rects.client.top );
 
-        SERVER_START_REQ( update_window_zorder )
+        /* An exposed part is taken to be uncovered on the screen, and the window is put above
+         * whatever the Win32 side has there.  With a compositing manager it is only the window
+         * asking for its contents: when the screen changed and every window was resized at
+         * once, that turned the Z order upside down under the window that had the focus. */
+        if (!is_screen_composited( event->display ))
         {
-            req->window      = wine_server_user_handle( hwnd );
-            req->rect        = wine_server_rectangle( abs_rect );
-            wine_server_call( req );
+            SERVER_START_REQ( update_window_zorder )
+            {
+                req->window      = wine_server_user_handle( hwnd );
+                req->rect        = wine_server_rectangle( abs_rect );
+                wine_server_call( req );
+            }
+            SERVER_END_REQ;
         }
-        SERVER_END_REQ;
     }
     else flags &= ~RDW_ALLCHILDREN;
 
